{
  "name": "prepare",
  "about": "Preparing the ask-first Space while the person is in onboarding: the Linux runtime, the agent image, the home Space and the coding agent start at first launch, say honestly where they are, carry on after a lost connection or a quit, queue the message the person sends meanwhile and deliver it exactly once when the agent is ready. Times are made up (milliseconds). Each step also shows what a list (Spaces, sidebar, machines, palette) shows of a roster of five Spaces: the home that warms for Home's prompt box is left out until a person has written into it, and comes back when one did.",
